- Cerulean Tower Tokyu Hotel (Shibuya)
  - Large rooms, strong value for size, convenient for exploring Shibuya and beyond; many rooms can couple with extra beds or sofa beds.

Near Tokyo Station / Ginza / central hubs
- The Tokyo Station Hotel (Marunouchi)
  - Classic luxury with direct access to Tokyo Station; easiest if you’re using the JR network; some family-friendly rooms and suites; very convenient for day trips.
- Mitsui Garden Hotel Kyobashi Tokyo Station
  - Comfortable, clean, good value; walkable to Tokyo Station and Ginza; family-friendly options.
- Imperial Hotel Tokyo (Taito area / closer to Hibiya)
  - Iconic luxury with renowned service; family rooms and connecting rooms available; prime central location.

Mid-range / good value
- Keio Plaza Hotel Tokyo (Shinjuku)
  - Very family-friendly, with connecting rooms and larger family rooms; easy access to multiple subway lines; solid value for central Tokyo.
- Grand Nikko Tokyo Daiba (Ariake / Odaiba)
  - Large rooms and suites, sister to many family-friendly amenities in Odaiba; good for families wanting space and a mix of indoor/outdoor activities nearby.

Tips for booking with kids
- Look for “family room,” “connecting rooms,” or “suite” options to get two sleeping areas.
- Check if the hotel offers cribs or extra beds and whether there are additional charges for children.
- Proximity to a station can save you time with little ones; Tokyo’s rail network is very kid-friendly if you’re using JR or subway lines.
- If you’re planning day trips (e.g., Disney, Nikko, Hakone), consider a base with easy access to major train hubs.

